WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.170
So basically, you're feeling unconfident.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.000
Because if I lose, I'll never be able to recover.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:07.960
Okay, look--

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.090
It was completely seasonally inappropriate,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.260
but it was still a <i>really</i> well-done lunch box!

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:18.640
A-And Mr. Maou and the others could be in danger if she poisoned it, you know?

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.140
If she's an Ente Isla assassin, the job's already done.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.600
Yes.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:29.900
Chiho, don't use us as a lame excuse. Go at this head-on.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.950
R-Right...

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.780
Coming!

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:39.740
My goodness.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.450
Good Sadao, you have a visitor.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.080
--'Kay, hold on a sec. Who is it? The MHK?
--S-S-S-S-S-S-S-S-Sadao?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.250
--No, it's the good Emi.
--Chiho?!

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.040
--Again?!
--S-S-S-S-S-Sadao?

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:03.640
<i>Kono shunkan, kono basho ga sutaato</i>

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:09.690
<i>Imeeji shite miyou naniga dekiru no ka na</i>

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.650
<i>Shinjirarenai dekigoto datte aru</i>

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.370
<i>Motto... koete yukeru ne</i>

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:30.340
<i>Zero kara umareru subete kagayaite ano sora e</i>

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.800
<i>Omoikiri habatakitai</i>

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:41.930
<i>Saikou no sumairu de warainagara saa yukou!</i>

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:47.770
<i>Michi no sekai e to ima tobidasou yo</i>

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:52.440
<i>Mirai wo erabi, kimeru no wa jibun</i>

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.740
<i>Yume wo oikakete yukou</i>

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.360
<i>Naku hi mo aru</i>

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.620
<i>Sore wa daiji na negai, kienaide</i>

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:10.540
<i>Kitto aeru kara, asu no kimi e...</i>

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.810
What? So you've been cooking for
Mr. Ashiya while he has heat fatigue?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.060
Now I see!

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:35.400
Wow, that perilla is chopped so thinly! It's really pretty!

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.990
It's easy if you slice it in half first, then gather it in a bunch before you julienne it.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.660
How did you get the lettuce so crisp?

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:46.160
After you give it a good washing, you just have to shake off the water.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.420
Really? I'm so impressed, Miss Suzuno!

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.630
Sure is crowded in here. Will we have enough bowls and chopsticks?

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.670
Oh, I brought mine with me.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.180
Oh. Okay, then I'll accept this with thanks!

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:04.390
And Miss Kamazuki helping too...
I'm so sorry for the trouble.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.060
Oh, breakfast already?

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.890
Wait, where am I supposed to sit?

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.860
I'll go delinquent on you.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.780
And why do I rate below Yusa, anyway?!

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.440
Guests first.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.700
And these are the bowls from that Sugiya takeout!

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.820
Bon appétit!

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.030
--Bon appétit!
--Hey!

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.540
Wow, I want to become a great cook like you, Miss Suzuno.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.660
I'm sure you'll progress quickly.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.080
You really think so?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.040
As for me, it sounds nice to say
I'm "treating them to home cooking,"

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.970
but really I'm just being pushy and making them help me use up my noodles.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.680
--I bought in bulk to be frugal until I find a job,
--Wait, I thought we had some fried fish?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.180
--but I might not be able to eat it all before it spoils in the heat.
--Hey, didn't we?

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.100
--What jobs are you considering, by the way?
--I know I saw some. I know I did.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.940
--I won't be unreasonable and ask for a full-time job.
--There was fried fish, right? Come on! Fried fish!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.150
--There was, right? Or did I imagine it?

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.900
--If I can make enough money

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.150
--to cover minimal living expenses by going into service, that's enough.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.740
--Who says "going into service" these days?
--There was some, right?

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.150
Why not come to MgRonald's, then?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:07.040
Chi's there too, so you won't have to be too stressed during your training.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.830
Sure, that won't be stressful, but there'll be <i>other</i> stress.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.960
Lots of shifts are understaffed lately, so we'd like the help.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.380
Anybody'd notice how the high school girl feels about this!

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.760
Don't you think so, Chi?

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.050
Huh?!

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.090
Um... y-yes.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.140
This is hopeless.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.060
Well, no need to make a snap decision!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:32.190
There are as many minuses to working with people you know as there are pluses!

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:36.020
Thank you, good Sadao.
I'll consider it as an option.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.650
I may end up asking for help later.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.030
Sure, okay.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.990
If so, I'll appreciate your help too, good Chiho.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.990
O-Okay...

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.780
The job is important, but for now,

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:52.120
why not help her with her clothes and belongings?

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:57.460
True, my dresser is rather bare, and I lack any purses or shoes.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.670
Wait, don't tell me you've only got traditional Japanese clothes?

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.050
I have no Western-style clothing.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.220
I-Is there something strange about that?

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:09.640
Well, I don't know about "strange," but...

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.770
Yusa, you know where they sell stuff like this, right?

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.600
Hey! No touching without permission!
You'll infect me with NEET-ness!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:15.690
It ain't infectious!

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.070
You never feel any shame about doing that stuff, do you, Mr. Urushihara?

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:22.320
What's your problem?!
Why is everybody so mean to me?!

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.740
Miss Yusa, why don't you take her to some clothing stores?

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.320
Okay, if we can do it after work...

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:31.910
I'll wander around the shopping area until you're finished, then.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.040
--Good idea.
--Yeah, good idea!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.870
Best not to take the risk, if you ask me...

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.500
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.550
Er...

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.590
Did you just change clothes?

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.010
Yes.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.600
She really <i>does</i> only have traditional clothes.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.680
Is something wrong?

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.640
No, forget it.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.020
Shall we go?

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.100
All right, sorry to visit so early.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.820
Get well soon, Mr. Ashiya.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:05.150
Thank you for the wonderful food.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.240
Now, Sire, you be sure to escort Miss Sasaki back home.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.740
What are you, my old lady?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.580
Your bike--

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:16.870
Dullahan.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.790
Right. It doesn't have a carrier on the back, huh?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.670
But utility bikes hardly ever do, right?

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.050
It's kind of a shame.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:27.180
A second rider gets you a fine of up to 20,000 yen in the city, you know.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:32.390
Of course I know. But that's not my point...

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:36.480
Say, Chi, didn't your parents have anything to say

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.020
about you visiting a bachelor pad?

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:44.190
Not particularly. I was honest about where I was going, after all.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.150
We've got Mom's approval, as they say!

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.200
A-And your dad?

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:54.910
Dad said, "So, you've already found a man you want to cook for?"

00:06:55.120 --> 00:07:00.000
Oh, what are you going to do for lunch, since Miss Suzuno's out?

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.210
Do? Uh, I haven't really thought about it--

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.800
In that case, is it all right if I bring you lunch?

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:11.680
Well, um... Ashiya would feel better about me eating your home cooking

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:15.140
than living on junk food, so...

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.970
I guess I'll take you up on that.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:21.020
Yay! I'll have to make sure it's nutritionally balanced, then,

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:23.480
so that he'll feel safe!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:27.740
Look, Chi... Doesn't it bother you that we're...?

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.910
That you're demons from another world?

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.820
Well, yeah.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:37.200
True, I'd be lying if I said it didn't bother me.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.870
Miss Yusa and I have been texting each other,

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.790
so I know a little about what you've done.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.760
But I fell for you before
I knew about that, Mr. Maou.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:55.890
Don't make that pathetic face!
Are you really aiming for world conquest?

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.970
But it's just--

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:03.270
Miss Yusa tried to stop me, so that I wouldn't have to regret falling for you.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.770
But I fell for you on my own.

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:10.610
So when I stop liking you,
I'll do that on my own, too.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:16.490
Even if you only think of me as your junior coworker, it's no big deal.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:22.210
Because it doesn't have anything to do with me liking you.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:26.460
Jeez, this is what makes humans so scary.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:27.630
That's right!

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.720
Especially girls--take us lightly and you'll <i>wish</i> you'd only been maimed!

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.390
I'll keep that in mind.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.430
You're truly loved, good Sadao.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.140
M-M-M-Miss Suzuno!
H-H-How long have you been there?!

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:44.850
Since somewhere around "I fell for you."

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:49.980
I think you're very virtuous, and cute, for being so honest about your feelings.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.360
--Regardless of whom you've picked.
--Huh?!

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.450
Chi?!

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:00.750
Aw, jeez. I hope she doesn't get into an accident going that fast.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.040
You surprise me.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.830
Is it really so surprising that
I'd worry about somebody?

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.960
Apologies, but yes.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.420
What are your thoughts on having a person like you?

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.220
Huh? Why the interrogation?

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:15.800
Oh, there's no deep meaning behind it...

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:20.680
Well, let's see. After she was so direct about it,

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:23.520
I don't wanna just pretend I don't get it.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:27.730
Plus, Chi--more like her parents-- well, her <i>mom</i> trusts me,

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:31.570
so I figure I gotta show my good faith... Hey!

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:32.740
What's with that look?

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.490
Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.950
Ah, that's right, I've kept the good Emi waiting.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.700
You're going to the station, right? I'll walk you there.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.160
Wh-What?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:48.210
No... nothing...

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.760
Find your wallet?

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:58.590
Y-Yeah, I'm okay.
I've kept you waiting; I'm sorry.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.140
Oh, no big deal.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:05.560
Er, so are we about to ride what they call a "train"?

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:11.400
Well, yes. We're only one stop from
Shinjuku, but it's a bit far to walk.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:16.450
Yes, about that... I've never been on a train.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:19.070
Huh?

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:22.620
I've heard that in Tokyo one pays for travel in watermelons.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.750
Where can I obtain one?

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:29.710
U-Um, wait a second.
Can I ask you something first?

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.170
How the heck did you get to Sasazuka?

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:36.220
I came here directly through the Gate.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:39.090
Oh, that explains--

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:42.010
Did you just say "Gate"?

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:44.850
Are you... from Ente Isla?

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:48.190
Wait, didn't you know that?

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:50.980
Huh?!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.450
You didn't say a word about that!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.160
<i>You</i> did! You asked if I was after the Devil!

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:07.250
And then you told me it would end badly if I got close to him,

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:09.500
and as a favor you warned me to steer clear!

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.960
Huh?!

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:14.170
So even though I've survived countless wars,

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:17.210
I knew I had to withdraw because <i>you,</i> the hero, rated him so dangerous!

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:20.550
But when I asked for help because I had nowhere to go if I left right away,

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.260
you pledged your aid and gave me your contact information!

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.770
What?!

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:29.810
Didn't you say those nice things because you intuited who I was?!

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:32.520
How could I possibly intuit that?!

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:34.650
Didn't it strike you as odd?!

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.400
A sweet young girl such as myself who just moved in,

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:41.660
--Who calls <i>herself</i> that?!
--venturing into an all-male home and slaving away for them? It's ridiculous!

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.740
Hearing that from <i>you</i> is seriously irritating!

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:49.080
Then what exactly were you thinking when you asked me if I was "after" him?!

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:58.670
Huh? Wait... Wh-Why did you ask if I had a "very close" relationship with him...?

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:02.220
Because I was told you'd joined forces with him!

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:04.800
Th-That's a load of crap!

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.470
We were just forced to take down

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:09.060
a <i>coincidentally</i> shared enemy together, that's all!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.140
So don't talk like that, it's just stupid!

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:15.560
Don't tell me you actually thought
I was conspiring with the Devil

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.320
to get revenge on the Church?!

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:21.860
It was <i>you</i> who sneak-attacked the convenience store yesterday, wasn't it?

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:23.660
Seaweed snacked?

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.410
Grrr!

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:28.700
I got attacked by someone from Ente Isla.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:33.170
They had the power to neutralize my sacred sword, so they weren't a demon.

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.790
Which means it had to have been you--

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.460
Huh?

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:41.510
She doesn't have any paintball marks, and she doesn't smell!

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:47.140
I did no such thing! I know how powerful the hero Emilia is!

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:52.730
Who are you, then, and why are you hanging around the Devil's Castle?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:56.060
My real name is Crestia Bel.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:13:00.070
I'm head investigator of the
Doctrinal Correction Council.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:04.740
If you still intend to defeat Satan, join us and--

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.160
Wait!

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:11.160
I don't want to be late for work, so save the details for Shinjuku, okay?

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:13.500
This is just how Japan works.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:18.170
Release me! I-I cannot afford to dawdle here!

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.880
Do you insist on hindering me?!

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.110
I can't believe you actually said "There are people inside this little panel!"

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.200
when you saw a flat screen TV.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:49.870
Please, let's drop that subject!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.250
How the heck did you study Japan, anyway?

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:56.290
After I realized yukata and kimono were the traditional Japanese dress,

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.340
I studied something called "historical drama," which features the most kimono.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:05.380
And also a documentary on the Showa period, the longest era in modern Japan.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:06.590
Now I see.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:10.800
My favorites are <i>O-arashi Monjiro,</i>
<i>Lone Lion and Cub,</i>

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:14.180
and ronin shows like <i>Three for the Slay</i>!

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:19.730
Things like <i>Mito Fukushogun</i> and
<i>Okorinbo Shogun</i> didn't really resonate.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:24.030
Uh-huh... So, getting back on topic,

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.820
why did the Doctrinal Correction
Council's head investigator

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.910
move next door to the Devil's Castle?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.370
All I learned from investigating Olba Mayer

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:37.870
was where Satan lived and what sort of lifestyle he had.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:40.040
I thought if I kept tabs on the Devil...

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.630
...the hero would eventually show up.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.710
So, what did you want with me?

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.680
First let me say one thing.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:53.310
I cannot apologize enough for
Olba Mayer's immoral acts against you.

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:56.730
From your attitude toward me before you knew I was Ente Islan,

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:02.690
I can see that the story of you joining the Devil was probably incorrect.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.400
Olba's will is not the Church's collective will.

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:09.280
I, at least, would like to be on your side.

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:12.780
Olba isn't important now. Let's cut to the chase.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:18.210
I want you to take down King Satan with me, and then return to Ente Isla.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:22.540
The Church would make your survival known, but cover up Olba's wrongdoing.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:24.250
Will you set them straight?

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:25.710
No way.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:29.550
I'm trying to restore your proper status and honor here!

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.970
I don't particularly care what the
Church or the kingdoms think of me.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:38.390
But I'm sure you can understand why
I can't just up and trust someone

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.560
from an organization led in part by the same guy

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:44.110
who caved in a crowded underground mall

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:48.190
just to kill me and the Devil.

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.450
Emerada and Albert could tell you how much trouble

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:56.660
Olba caused this country with
Lucifer in order to kill me.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.660
Or you can ask Urushihara himself.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:04.290
Besides--taking down the
Devil is my job as a hero.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:05.880
Don't interfere.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.000
Then if we cooper--

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:12.590
The old Inquisition, now known as the "Doctrinal Correction Council."

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.930
You're with them, and you still don't get it?

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:20.270
Oh, and I don't know why you're giving them food aid,

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.650
but I'll warn you of one thing:

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:27.020
if you mess with him or play any cheap tricks, he'll see right through you.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:29.900
He may not look it, but he <i>is</i> the Devil.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.450
I... appreciate your warning.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:36.620
Still, you've got your own position to think about, right?

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:40.540
I grabbed this at the station for you. And this, too.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:46.080
If you're going to be here a while, learn a little more about the place.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:50.760
The way you dress and talk is just way too old-fashioned.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:56.850
Okay, I have to go to work now.
Let's save the rest for after my shift.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.430
I'm so sorry!

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:02.230
F-For what?

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.600
I-I... stole your bike...

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.060
Oh, that.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:10.320
--I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry...!
--No, it's okay. It's <i>okay</i>!

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:15.570
It's as slow here today as I figured.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:19.450
The new SFC across the street took all our customers.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:24.290
And Miss Kisaki's got a <i>super</i> dangerous smile on her face...

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.170
I'm skiin' without a jacket.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:29.590
Our sales've dropped over 80% since yesterday.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:33.380
Why do I have to go to headquarters <i>today</i>?

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:37.850
Once, somebody hired in my year lost a fierce competition with her rival

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:40.810
and got packed off to Greenland.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:42.770
For real?

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:46.100
No way do we want to go to Greenland, right?

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:47.270
Right!

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.650
I don't care what you have to do.
I authorize any means necessary!

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.070
Defeat SFC!

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.530
Yes, Ma'am!

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:01.790
Dang it! I can't believe <i>this</i> is my first day as substitute manager...

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.370
Welcome!

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:08.630
Excuse me, I know you're busy.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.960
Is the manager here?

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:15.920
I'm sorry, but Manager Kisaki isn't here today.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:18.930
I'd be happy to assist you in her place.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:23.680
Sadao Maou, I presume?
I've heard a lot about you.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:26.770
Hardworking, sociable, and broad-minded...

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:30.560
I hear you have a wonderful human touch in everything.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:33.150
Er, I'm flattered.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.740
Does this guy need help?

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:38.820
Oh dear, excuse me. Here is my card.

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.660
Oh, thank you.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:45.160
The manager of Sentucky Fried Chicken?!

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:51.000
The name is Mitsuki Sarue. I'm sorry for not coming to greet you sooner.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.500
I've been so busy, you see.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:56.340
I have to say, Hatagaya is a nice neighborhood.

00:18:56.550 --> 00:19:00.430
It's right between the residential and business areas, so the demographics are excellent.

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.850
All the women are gorgeous.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:03.970
Right.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:07.520
Well, let's do our best as fellow workers in the station shopping arcade.

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:10.020
Hmm.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:16.150
Well! It's a shame I can't see your famously ravishing manager, bu--what?!

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.400
Gorgeous.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.740
Please, use those graceful hands of yours

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.620
to make a to-go meal just for me...

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.620
...my young lady.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:37.800
Sorry, Chi. I should've put a stop to that creeper.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.300
No, Mr. Maou, it wasn't your fault!

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:43.350
I'm just disgusted with that little shrimp of a manager!

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:48.430
Heavy cologne and sunglasses? I question that in a customer service worker!

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.140
I'm <i>not</i> going to lose to him!

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:52.190
--That's the spirit.
--Huh?

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:56.230
We'll have info on the enemy soon. I sent in a spy.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:57.820
A spy?

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:00.860
As my king bids it,

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:06.870
I shall thoroughly investigate that "Sentucky Fried Chicken" place!

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:12.330
--Boy, I'm starving!
--Good Emi.

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:17.050
Good Emi, you've finished your service at last?

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.840
So you ended up buying more yukata...

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:22.180
Did you have that much money?

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:28.640
I had some easily converted assets, so I sold a few at a shop called Mugihyo.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:31.180
Th-Th-This is...!

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:34.980
I just hope you didn't sell any valuables for a song...

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.770
I managed to buy it! Impressed?

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:40.990
Um...

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:44.950
Please enter your payment, making sure to check the amount.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:52.500
If you require a receipt, please press the receipt button.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:55.040
Wh-What more do you want?!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.540
Great job, kid.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:58.960
Say, is this a friend of yours?

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:02.880
Um, well, I guess you could say that...

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:06.680
I waited here because I have another request for you, good Emi.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:07.930
What is it?

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:10.430
I wish to go see the good Sadao's workplace.

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:12.730
--Would you accompany me?
--H-H-Hey!

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.400
"Sadao"? I feel like I know that name...

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:18.230
--I know you don't want me getting close to him,
--Whoa, hey!

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.110
but I can't just stand down.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:22.440
Huh? What does she mean? Hey, what's up?

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.860
--Did I stumble into a bloodbath here?!
--I knew this would happen...

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:31.290
Hey, I know I'm butting in here, but you usually can't resolve these things alone!

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:34.540
--You need a third party to be the judge, you know?!
--I'm telling you, Rika, it's not like that!

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.920
You need help. I'll tag along!

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:38.960
So, where is this Mr. Sadao?

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:40.840
At the Hatagaya MgRonald's...

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:43.920
--Hey, w-wait!
--Aw, we can get there by train in no time!

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.720
<i>I'm</i> not going, got it?!

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:23.590
<i>Doko kara asa ni naru? Shizuka na sora</i>

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:29.140
<i>Minai furi wo shita yubikiri koyubi no saki</i>

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:39.340
<i>Warawareta tsuki nara kiete</i> <i>yuku n da kinou no houkaku e</i>

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:45.280
<i>Usotsuki okubyoumono</i> <i>minna matomete boku nara</i>

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:51.070
<i>Saite ita no wa yume no naka da</i>

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:56.540
<i>Tsuki no kage ni kakushiteta</i> <i>hontou wa ne naiteta</i>

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:02.250
<i>Namida wa mou nagarenai karete shimatta no?</i>

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:08.880
<i>Nani mo ka mo yurusetara</i> <i>nagareru ka mo shirenai kedo</i>

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:16.430
<i>Mamoritai mono bakari da na</i>

00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:40.960
"The Hero Experiences a Fray"
